AudD  ·  profile default
                 │ Help › Keys
 1 Recognize     │  Getting started  Guide  Commands >Keys< Exit codes  Links 
 2 Now playing   │ Moving around
 3 Streams       │   Menu on the left, page on the right. Arrows move, Enter
 4 Recognitions  │   goes in, Esc comes back.
 5 Account       │   The menu is the sidebar; Help, Streams, Recognitions, and
 6 Settings      │   Account have a tab bar above their page. On a choice ‹ like
*7 Help          >   this ›, ←/→ change it and ← on its first option goes back.
                 │   While you type in a field, letters and digits go into it:
                 │   esc leaves the field, ctrl+u clears it. What a page can do
                 │   is on its buttons: tab (or ↓ from the end of the page)
                 │   reaches them, ←/→ move between them, enter presses one. A
                 │   letter on a button, such as (o), presses it from anywhere
                 │   on the page. A key works only where it is listed; any other
                 │   key says it does nothing. A question is a dialog with
                 │   Cancel first: enter presses the focused button, y confirms,
                 │   n or esc cancels. 1-7 jump to a section except while you
                 │   type in a field.
 ctrl+k commands │ 
 ? keys  q quit  │ ↓ 105 more lines below

←/→ tabs  ↓ open  esc back  ? keys
ctrl+k runs any audd command